{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792231987,"nonce":"L7XicdndQ8WCKZb/ykpb1pTP184=","title":"Run ashui in a browser through Ash's wasm target","message":"**Goal**\n\nashui programs run in a page, for the web showcase on the launch website. Ash builds HashLink bytecode for wasm32-wasip1-threads and hosts it in a page; ashui needs its native part and its Haxe code to work there.\n\n**What already exists**\n\n- Ash loads wasm side modules in a page (d19312b) and has a window protocol over shared memory (a29201b8, docs/wasm/window.md). Native .hdll files do not load there.\n- hlwgpu ships xgpu.wasm and its WebGPU agent, hlwindow ships xwindow.wasm. hlwindow's scripts/gpu_test.sh builds and runs a window plus GPU page under Ash; it is the recipe for an ashui page.\n- The browser host has no filesystem: path_open answers ENOTSUP.\n\n**Verified 2026-10-17**\n\n- blinc_abi compiles for wasm32-wasip1-threads and links as blinc_abi.wasm with the recipe hlwgpu and hlwindow use: a position-independent std from build-std, hl_abi's ProgramAllocator as the global allocator, a local TLS errno slot, and --unresolved-symbols=import-dynamic for blinc_abi's own cdylib link. scripts/build_wasm.sh does it; the module is 6.7 MB with LTO off.\n- ashui's smoke bytecode lowers to wasm: 3011 of 3011 functions, none refused.\n- Blocker in Ash: blinc_abi.wasm imports libm functions the runtime object does not define (acosf, atan2f, cosf, exp2f, hypotf, log2, log2f, powf and two more), so ash --build refuses it. The libm entry points belong in LIBRARY_LIBC in scripts/build_wasm_runtime.py. The module's full libm imports are acos, acosf, atan2, atan2f, cos, cosf, exp2f, hypotf, log2, log2f, pow, powf, sin, sinf, tan, tanf.\n\n**Remaining work, in order**\n\n- Ash libm entry points (blocked on the Ash session), then run the smoke test and the suites as wasm under ash run.\n- Audit the Haxe side for what a page lacks: file reads at run time (stylesheets, bitmaps, fonts, snapshot and debug tools), sys.io.Process in Platform, and anything else that assumes a desktop. Guard with #if wasm, or embed at compile time.\n- Fonts: blinc_text has no system fonts in a page, so the fonts are embedded or fetched.\n- WindowedApp on xwindow.wasm and xgpu.wasm, and the page that loads them with blinc_abi.wasm.\n- A build script and a CI job for the showcase page.\n\n**Shipping**\n\nOnce the wasm target is stable, the published packages carry blinc_abi.wasm and the installer macro installs it: a wasm entry in native/hdlls.json, scripts/package_haxelib.py and the release workflow building and packing it, and NativeInstall.stage copying it beside the output when the program is built for wasm. Say whether hlwgpu's and hlwindow's wasm modules ship in ashui's package or stay in their own zips.","files":null}]}